-- title:
--   Local twisted orbital mass over the integral-determinant order
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ an extension of $K$ of degree $2$, and let $\sigma$ be a $K$-automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-automorphism of $L$ lies in the group generated by $\sigma$. Let $\delta_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$, let $c$ be a unit of $L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K$ and $u$ an idelic unit of $K$, and put $\delta = \delta_0 \cdot \mathrm{scalar}(c)$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K)$, where $\delta_0$ is mapped in by $\ell \mapsto \ell \otimes 1$. Assume the norm string of $\delta$, that is the product $\prod_{i<[L:K]} \sigma_{\mathrm{GL}}^{i}(\delta)$ with $\sigma_{\mathrm{GL}}$ induced by $\sigma \otimes \mathrm{id}$, equals the scalar matrix with entries $1 \otimes u$ (`hN`), and that no $K$-rational twisted conjugate $x^{-1}\delta_0\,\sigma(x)$, $x \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$, is a scalar matrix $\mathrm{scalar}(z)$ with $z \in L^\times$. Fix a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_K$ and write $\delta_v$ for the image of $\delta$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$, $q_v = \mathrm{absNorm}(v)$, $T_v = \{t : t\,\delta_v\,\sigma_{\mathrm{GL}}(t)^{-1} = \delta_v\}$ the twisted centralizer of $\delta_v$, and $S = \{t \in T_v : \det t = 1 \otimes s$ for some $s \in K_v^\times$ with $|s|_v = 1\}$. Let $\tau$ be a Haar measure on $T_v$ and $t_v \in [0,\infty]$ with $\tau(S)\, q_v = t_v + \tau(S)$, and assume $\delta_v$ is not $\sigma$-conjugate to any scalar matrix over $L \otimes_K K_v$. Assume further that the twisted commutant $\{X \in M_2(L) : X\delta_0 = \delta_0\,\sigma(X)\}$ is the $K$-span of a finite $K$-linearly independent family $b$. Then $$\int_{\{t \in T_v \,:\, t \in \Lambda\}} \bigl\| N_{(L\otimes_K K_v)/K_v}(\det t)\bigr\|\, d\tau(t) = t_v\,(q_v-1)^{-1}\,\bigl(1-q_v^{-2}\bigr)^{-1},$$ where $\Lambda$ is the additive subgroup of $M_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ generated by those $X$ with $X\delta_v = \delta_v\,(\sigma\otimes\mathrm{id})(X)$ and $\det X = 1 \otimes a$ for some $a$ in the valuation ring of $K_v$, and the integrand is the lower Lebesgue integral of $\mathrm{ofReal}\,\|\cdot\|$ of the algebra norm of the determinant.
--
--   This is the local mass computation at a finite place $v$ of the second kind: the $\| N \det \|_v$-weighted volume of the integral-determinant order inside the twisted centralizer, expressed as $t_v q_v^{-1}\zeta_v(1)\zeta_v(2)$ in the normalisation fixed by the shell condition on $\tau$. It is used in the computation of twisted (base-change) orbital integrals, and is cited by [`AutomorphicForm.setLIntegral_lattice_norm_det_mul_norm_four_eq_mul_sqrt_norm_det_trace_of_not_isSigmaConjugate_scalar`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.setLIntegral_lattice_norm_det_mul_norm_four_eq_mul_sqrt_norm_det_trace_of_not_isSigmaConjugate_scalar).
